WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.390
- A massive and coordinated
effort to steal this election.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.360
- Electoral fraud that
would be perpetrated

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.620
through electronic voting.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.520
- They used the machines to
trash large batches of votes.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.320
- [Narrator] Claims like
these are at the center

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.370
of a $1.6 billion defamation
case against Fox News.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.910
Dominion Voting Systems
sued the broadcaster in 2021

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.490
over alleged defamatory on-air comments

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.230
that tied the company's voting machines

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.990
to false claims of election fraud in 2020.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.770
- This case really examines
that line between what is

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.570
journalism and what should be protected

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.130
and what shouldn't be.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.690
- [Narrator] From internal text messages

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.520
to high profile depositions,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.720
here's what you need
to know about the case.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.480
During the 2020 presidential
election, voting machine maker

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.240
Dominion had contracts in 28 states.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.580
And after former president
Donald Trump lost,

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.920
Fox had his associates on broadcasts.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.743
- Sidney Powell and Rudy Giuliani

00:00:54.743 --> 00:00:57.270
claiming that Dominion rigged the election

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.030
in favor of President Joe Biden.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.740
- [Narrator] Federal and
state officials have said

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.410
there is no evidence that
any voting system deleted

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.960
or changed votes during the 2020 election.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.390
The company argues that
by airing those claims,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.382
Fox News gave them prominence,
even though they were false.

00:01:12.382 --> 00:01:14.100
Fox says that it was reporting

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.200
on newsworthy claims
from a sitting President

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.380
and his associates that other
media outlets also covered.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.970
Dominion's main argument is that

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.550
Fox News knowingly broadcast false claims

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.570
about its machines,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.000
because it had a financial
incentive to do so.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.190
Fox has denied that allegation.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.440
- Many executives in a lot

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.270
of these email communications
were expressing

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.240
a lot of angst about losing viewership.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.370
- [Narrator] So Dominion
alleges that Fox leaned

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.560
into the false claims to keep its viewers.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.050
In released court filings,
Dominion says that

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.230
internal communications
among Fox hosts and staff

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.472
prove that Fox knew the claims were false,

00:01:48.472 --> 00:01:51.600
like a text message from
Tucker Carlson to his producer,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.760
which said, "Sidney Powell is lying."

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.017
And another one he sent
to Laura Ingram that said,

00:01:56.017 --> 00:01:58.050
"It's unbelievably offensive to me.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.450
Our viewers are good people
and they believe it."

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.360
And in her deposition,
Fox host Maria Bartiromo

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.700
called an email regarding
the election fraud claims

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.280
from Powell, "Kooky and unreliable."

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.830
But on her show a day after
receiving the email...

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.500
- Sidney, we talked about
the Dominion software.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.620
I know that there were
voting irregularities.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.793
Tell me about that.

00:02:19.463 --> 00:02:21.030
- That's to put it mildly.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.730
The computer glitches
could not and should not

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.672
have happened at all.

00:02:26.672 --> 00:02:29.100
That is where the fraud took place,

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.510
where they were flipping votes

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:34.260
in the computer system or
adding votes that did not exist.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.710
- All of these domain will use to say Fox

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.213
had a disregard for the facts of the case.

00:02:41.213 --> 00:02:43.650
- [Narrator] Fox says
that its on-air hosts

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.740
didn't make the Dominion
election fraud claims themselves.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.660
Dominion also released a deposition

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.060
from Fox Corporation
Chairman Rupert Murdoch,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.530
who also owns News Corp,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.510
the parent company of
the Wall Street Journal.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.690
- He did acknowledge that
some of the broadcast

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.500
did endorse claims of a false election

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.930
as opposed to simply reporting on them,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.013
and he acknowledged that
he could have stopped

00:03:07.013 --> 00:03:08.130
it from happening.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.800
Fox says that these
quotes were cherry picked

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.917
from the deposition, but
those statements on their own,

00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:16.164
Dominion will try to use to show that

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:18.480
executives like Rupert Murdoch,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.930
had control over these
decisions that were made on air.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.640
- [Narrator] The judge
said prior to the trial

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.990
that he would require Murdoch

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.240
and other Fox Corp executives to testify,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.980
if Dominion subpoenaed them.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.600
In a statement, Fox said

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.550
demanding witnesses who had nothing to do

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.520
with the challenged broadcasts
is just the latest example

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.840
of their political crusade

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.700
in search of a financial windfall.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.060
Fox also says the lawsuit is
an attack on press freedom.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.130
The 1964 Supreme Court case,

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.810
New York Times versus Sullivan,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.030
says that plaintiffs suing for defamation

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:51.210
must be able to prove that the
publisher had actual malice.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.559
- Which means that you knew
that the information was wrong

00:03:53.559 --> 00:03:55.721
or you had a reckless
disregard for the truth

00:03:55.721 --> 00:03:57.090
in publishing it.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.250
- [Narrator] It's a
historically high bar to meet,

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.010
and Fox says that Dominion's
evidence doesn't clear it.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.587
- They say that some of the statements

00:04:04.587 --> 00:04:06.385
that have been highlighted,

00:04:06.385 --> 00:04:10.860
text messages expressing doubt
were simply cherry picked.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.220
They believe that the host did express,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.760
in some extent, expressed
enough skepticism on air.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.830
- Like here when Tucker Carlson said

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.860
he invited Powell to back
up her claims with evidence.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.690
- But she never sent us any evidence

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.350
despite a lot of requests,
polite requests, not a page.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.417
- [Narrator] Dominion says
that the emails, texts,

00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:33.330
and deposition testimony
speak for themselves.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.390
In late March, Judge
Eric Davis ruled the case

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.800
should go to a jury trial.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.220
- The judge also rejected
Fox's arguments that they

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.200
should be protected by
the First Amendment,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.871
and that they could have a shield

00:04:44.871 --> 00:04:47.310
for reporting allegations neutrally.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.020
- [Narrator] Fox says
that the newsworthiness

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.990
of the statements at issue
are clear and indisputable.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.150
The judge also said
that Dominion had proof

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.950
that claims the company
had rigged the election

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.360
for Joe Biden were false.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.080
Days before the trial was set to begin,

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.710
Judge Davis said he was
likely to investigate,

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.210
whether Fox News improperly

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.340
withheld information during litigation.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.830
He also said Fox might face sanctions.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.770
Fox News said it didn't
improperly withhold information

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.230
from Dominion and produced
additional materials,

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.180
when it became aware of them.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.610
So the trial will likely
focus on whether Dominion

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.951
can prove Fox acted with actual malice,

00:05:19.951 --> 00:05:22.980
and if it suffered financial
damages as a result.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.449
- This trial is a rare
example of a defamation case

00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:28.920
making it all the way to trial.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.660
And it's particularly important

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.180
because Fox News is a huge name in media,

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.760
and they have a lot of influence,

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.270
and so it'll be in some
ways a test of this

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.797
very difficult standard of defamation.

00:05:41.797 --> 00:05:44.056
(gentle music)

